# PWD: system/nfc

From 7d7c0323eb7b757da41c4d3a6756aee51101fd9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: antoniu200 <33966771+antoniu200@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 00:53:36 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: llcp: Fall back to GKI_BUF3_MAX when DYN_ALLOC has no
 pools

libnfc-nci is built with -DDYN_ALLOC=1, which sets
GKI_NUM_FIXED_BUF_POOLS to 0. GKI_poolcount(LLCP_POOL_ID) then
returns 0, so llcp_init() computes num_rx_buff, max_num_tx_buff and
the link-layer limits as 0. Every outgoing LLCP data PDU is then
treated as congested, and SNEP/handover replies never leave the
device (PeerToPeer::send blocks until the link drops).

If the pool count is 0 under DYN_ALLOC, use GKI_BUF3_MAX instead
(9 rx / 21 tx buffers).

Tested with Android Beam between two phones running this library:
SNEP Put in both directions completes (SendTask result=true on the
sender, onP2pReceiveComplete on the receiver). Handover (file/photo
transfer) and large payloads were not tested.

Change-Id: If865454c0ff7de54365c6dc49e6271846d46d32d
---
 src/nfc/llcp/llcp_main.cc | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/nfc/llcp/llcp_main.cc b/src/nfc/llcp/llcp_main.cc
index 1185e013..a1b31ab5 100644
--- a/src/nfc/llcp/llcp_main.cc
+++ b/src/nfc/llcp/llcp_main.cc
@@ -72,6 +72,12 @@ void llcp_init(void) {
 
   /* total number of buffers for LLCP */
   pool_count = GKI_poolcount(LLCP_POOL_ID);
+  
+#ifdef DYN_ALLOC
+  /* No fixed GKI pools with DYN_ALLOC: GKI_poolcount() is 0 and every LLCP
+   * tx/rx limit below collapses to 0. So use the size that pool 3 has otherwise. */
+  if (pool_count == 0) pool_count = GKI_BUF3_MAX;
+#endif
 
   /* number of buffers for receiving data */
   llcp_cb.num_rx_buff = (pool_count * LLCP_RX_BUFF_RATIO) / 100;

